for name,lines,assessment in [
 ('bottleneck_distance.rs',253,'Complete body read. Exhaustive partial matching plus diagonal option correctly covers finite ungraded diagrams of at most eight points, including unequal and equal cardinalities. It silently drops essential bars and ignores dimension labels, so the result concerns a finite ungraded projection. Rational costs become f64 with no rounding interval, underflow check or monitored error tolerance despite the profile comment and exact-matching wording. Reversed intervals are accepted through absolute diagonal cost. Existing tests correctly cover identical, empty and distant-diagonal cases, but omit grading, essential bars and representational extremes.'),
 ('wasserstein_distance.rs',229,'Complete body read. Exhaustive partial matching minimizes a sum of powers and takes its reciprocal root on at most six finite points per side. Reuses the finite ungraded floating costs and ignores essential points. Any finite q>0 is admitted, including q<1 where triangle inequality fails; no overflow/underflow error bound is returned. Generic capacity record is unrelated. The far-point q=1 test checks diagonal matching, not a general metric or error certificate.'),
 ('interleaving_distance.rs',181,'Complete body read. Shell plus exact ordered integer endpoint proximity under supplied epsilon. This is a sufficient endpoint-matching condition for intervals, not a general multi-parameter/zigzag interleaving computation or minimum including diagonal/zero matching. Checked signed subtraction can refuse a mathematically representable u64 gap at extreme i64 endpoints; conservative range refusal is explicit. Positive and unordered/wide-gap examples exercise the narrow predicate.'),
 ('diagram_plotting.rs',114,'Complete body read. Shell plus checked positive grid cell and horizontal/vertical adjacency capacities. Correct finite combinatorial count, but supplied arrow counts do not establish actual placements or a persistence diagram rendering. No plotting, coordinate transformation or global diagram validation occurs. Local capacity example and excess-horizontal refusal are meaningful.'),
 ('dipha_io.rs',159,'Complete body read. Shell plus safe sixteen-byte little-endian magic/type preamble parser for the locally enumerated codes. Short/magic/unsupported-type failures are explicit; extra bytes and payload are not validated. No read/write transport or interoperability proof is present. Tests cover one locally declared persistence code and a short buffer. External DIPHA specification was not consulted, so format-code compatibility is not independently certified.'),
 ('gudhi_io.rs',125,'Complete body read. Shell plus nonempty strictly increasing u32 vertex tuple and checked vertex-count-minus-one dimension. This is a narrow simplex shape predicate, not a Gudhi file parser, filtration or interoperability check. Tests exercise a triangle dimension and repeated-vertex refusal.'),
 ('perseus_io.rs',119,'Complete body read. Shell plus scalar counts for a codimension-one face/coface and birth monotonicity. No actual vertex sets or containment are inputs, so this verifies arithmetic and timestamps only. Checked additions/subtractions refuse overflow. No Perseus parser or external specification validation; local positive dimension and late-face tests are bounded.'),
 ('phat_io.rs',127,'Complete body read. Shell plus sorted unique indices strictly below their column index, with checked incidence counts. This is a useful upper-triangular representation gate, not a square-zero boundary or degree proof: columns [],[0],[1] satisfy it but their composed boundary is nonzero. No file transport/parser, payload binding or tests of the added operation appear in this body. No external PHAT compatibility certified.'),
 ('upper_triangular_pairs.rs',83,'Complete body read. Generates all i<j<n pairs; incremental append trusts the caller and can duplicate or skip pairs. Separate certify validates ordering, bounds, uniqueness and exact n(n-1)/2 cardinality, which together establish completeness over the declared finite universe. Intermediate product overflow is conservatively refused. Two local tests cover a complete triple and descending-pair refusal; no source mutation performed.'),
 ('matrix_reduction.rs',177,'Complete body read. Dense rank and product use explicit mod-two semantics and rectangular/composable shape checks. Independent exhaustive 3x3 binary census matches span-cardinality rank. Empty row representation loses zero-row column dimension, a representation limitation rather than a silently certified external matrix shape. Q implementation is not supplied despite broad module heading. Tests cover field semantics, cancellation and malformed shapes; shell label is separate.'),
 ('clearing_optimization.rs',206,'Complete body read. Exact local unit-pivot integer column update: validates lengths/pivot index, restricts pivot to +/-1, recomputes all claimed entries with checked arithmetic and requires pivot zero. Correct elementary operation conditional on supplied columns, not the persistent-homology clearing lemma or an optimized global reduction. The output retains only pivot/height rather than column/source identity. Meaningful positive and nonunit-refusal tests.'),
 ('twist_algorithm.rs',189,'Complete body read. Bounded row bitmasks (1..64) and trailing-one pivot elimination compute GF2 rank/nullity, with index checks, step bound and distinct final pivots. Independent 3x3 exhaustive comparison agrees with span rank. This is column elimination; it does not reconstruct persistent pairings, clearing order or the full named twist optimization. No boundary-square-zero premise is required for matrix rank itself. The single local rank-two example is narrow.'),
 ('representative_cycle.rs',125,'Complete body read. Public floating sparse record has no canonical support, finite checks, boundary binding or bar reconstruction; is_zero tests every listed coefficient individually and misses cancellation at repeated indices. Separate private Gf2Cycle checks sorted nonempty selected indices and parity cancellation of caller-supplied boundary lists with universe bounds; it proves kernel membership for that supplied matrix only, not nontrivial homology or persistence provenance. Zero support is intentionally refused. Triangle positive and two-edge negative examples meaningfully test parity.')]:a.record(b+name,1,lines,assessment)
